🔍 Deep Dive: Google Business Profile (GBP)

Your observation is accurate: having only one single 5-star review presents a significant trust barrier.
• The Trust Trap: Modern travellers assume a single five-star rating is written by the business owner or a friend. Without at least 10–15 unique reviews, potential guests will hesitate to book directly.
• Algorithm Disadvantage: Google's local algorithm prioritises Review Velocity (how frequently you get reviews) and Review Diversity. A stagnant profile will not rank in the coveted Google Maps "Top 3 Local Pack."
• The Silver Lining: The profile includes high-quality interior images and a connected website, meaning the technical foundation is already set up correctly.

🌐 Deep Dive: Search Engine Optimization (SEO)

• Keyword Cannibalisation: Searching for "Glover Apartments" frequently surfaces expensive real estate options on Glover Road in Ikoyi rather than this Ogudu location. Because "Glover" is a highly competitive real estate term in Lagos, the website struggles to rank on broad searches without geographical modifiers like "Ogudu shortlet".
• Lack of Local Citation Volume: Their Name, Address, and Phone number (NAP) data is published on travel aggregators like Skyscanner and Agoda. However, they lack strong local citations on Nigerian business directories (e.g., VConnect, BusinessList), which signals a low authority score to Google's search engine.

🚀 Recommended Fixes to Boost Rankings

• Implement a Review System: Place a QR code linked to the Google Maps Profile inside the apartments. Offer a small incentive (like a 5% discount on the next stay or a late checkout) for guests who leave an honest review before departing.
• Target Long-Tail Keywords: Optimize the website text for specific search intents, such as "affordable multi-bedroom shortlets in Ogudu GRA" or "serviced apartments near mainland Lagos."